WEBVTT

00:08.570 --> 00:15.770
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.570 --> 00:15.770
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.810 --> 00:22.520
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.810 --> 00:22.520
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.320 --> 00:31.120
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.320 --> 00:31.120
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:31.160 --> 00:35.830
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:31.160 --> 00:35.830
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.430 --> 00:44.830
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.430 --> 00:44.830
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.880 --> 00:52.510
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.880 --> 00:52.510
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.590 --> 01:01.790
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.590 --> 01:01.790
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.790 --> 01:08.930
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.790 --> 01:08.930
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:09.100 --> 01:16.230
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:09.100 --> 01:16.230
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.340 --> 01:23.840
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.340 --> 01:23.840
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:34.590 --> 01:36.390
I knew it...

01:36.990 --> 01:43.260
Saya appeared right by Ichika.

01:44.370 --> 01:47.700
I didn't want to believe it, however.

01:58.050 --> 02:01.410
But I don't want Ichika...

02:03.320 --> 02:04.840
...to have to go through what I did...

02:06.360 --> 02:07.560
Do you want it?

02:07.560 --> 02:09.860
Oh, I don't...

02:09.860 --> 02:11.690
Why don't I give it to you, Ichika?

02:14.100 --> 02:15.600
Are you sure?

02:15.600 --> 02:16.060
Yes.

02:20.640 --> 02:22.370
Thank you very much!

02:22.370 --> 02:24.570
I'll treasure it, I promise!

02:29.480 --> 02:32.070
This is all my fault.

02:32.810 --> 02:33.800
No, it's not.

02:34.680 --> 02:36.550
Don't get down only on yourself.

02:40.590 --> 02:43.580
I'm the one that should bear the responsibility.

02:43.660 --> 02:48.160
The Jealousy of a Twig

02:51.230 --> 02:53.960
It was a summer cold.

02:55.300 --> 02:58.770
When I felt I'd gotten better,

02:58.770 --> 03:02.300
this time it was Manatsu
who seemed to have caught it.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.310
I'm sorry, Ichika.

03:06.950 --> 03:07.880
I'm really...

03:08.850 --> 03:10.220
Don't worry.

03:10.790 --> 03:14.280
A doctor will be here soon.

03:23.100 --> 03:29.660
But I was worried whether a doctor
would be able to treat Manatsu,

03:30.410 --> 03:32.170
who came out from a mirror.

03:43.690 --> 03:45.050
Coming!

03:46.120 --> 03:48.750
I'm sorry for making you come out
all this way, Doctor.

04:01.540 --> 04:02.800
Stay well.

04:03.610 --> 04:06.340
It'll be quite a lot of trouble
if you go breaking on me again.

04:10.580 --> 04:13.880
Is there something odd about Manatsu?

04:14.150 --> 04:17.810
Oh nothing... Just a cold.

04:18.190 --> 04:22.690
She's quite weak, so I'm worried she might
catch pneumonia, however...

04:23.160 --> 04:24.680
But I think she'll be fine now.

04:25.090 --> 04:26.290
That's not it...

04:27.130 --> 04:31.530
I see girls come down with these sorts of
symptoms once every few years.

04:32.670 --> 04:35.400
Please come to get medication later,

04:35.400 --> 04:41.040
and make sure to bring her
medical insurance card then.

04:41.540 --> 04:43.980
Manatsu came out from a mirror!

04:43.980 --> 04:45.710
She doesn't have any health insurance!

04:45.710 --> 04:49.480
We will handle all the expenses
directly ourselves.

04:50.050 --> 04:53.390
She doesn't have her health insurance card.

04:53.820 --> 04:55.290
I understand.

04:55.290 --> 04:57.460
Then I'll prepare the prescription.

04:57.460 --> 04:59.060
Thank you.

04:59.060 --> 05:04.000
Mother... Could it be she knows about Manatsu?

05:08.140 --> 05:09.640
That's it!

05:09.640 --> 05:12.270
Thank you very much.

05:12.710 --> 05:14.040
Take care.

05:14.040 --> 05:15.180
Doctor!

05:15.180 --> 05:15.910
What is it?

05:18.080 --> 05:18.880
Um...

05:50.310 --> 05:53.340
An illness where your eyes shine in the dark?

05:55.650 --> 05:57.620
Your pupils dilate to take in
as much light as they can

05:57.620 --> 06:00.820
when you stay in the darkness for a while.

06:00.820 --> 06:03.460
In other words, the lens opens wide.

06:03.460 --> 06:06.830
When that happens, it looks like
your eyes are sparkling.

06:06.830 --> 06:08.230
It's not an illness.

06:08.230 --> 06:10.200
I see.

06:10.200 --> 06:15.360
It also happens when you're interested in
something or fall in love with someone, yes?

06:15.970 --> 06:19.460
Do you have a crush on someone, Ichika?

06:20.580 --> 06:22.910
I don't...

06:22.910 --> 06:24.500
Oh, really?

06:30.020 --> 06:33.420
This isn't what the doctor was talking about.

06:34.520 --> 06:36.290
This shining...

06:39.330 --> 06:44.130
This... must be...

07:04.750 --> 07:05.950
No!

07:07.460 --> 07:09.480
This isn't Manatsu's fault!

07:10.360 --> 07:13.350
It must be something else...

07:19.300 --> 07:21.470
It was then that I started feeling

07:21.470 --> 07:26.410
that I was changing more and more
since I met Manatsu.

07:27.110 --> 07:30.240
Scared of the changes I could not stop,

07:30.250 --> 07:33.410
it seemed like something
was overflowing within me...

07:45.190 --> 07:49.360
Huh? Why was I sleeping in Ichika's bed?

07:51.000 --> 07:52.370
Oh, right...

07:52.370 --> 07:54.200
A doctor saw me.

07:57.970 --> 08:03.940
Ichika must realize that
I don't have a normal body...

08:14.890 --> 08:17.060
An electric dryer is convenient,

08:17.060 --> 08:20.390
but you can't beat drying clothes
in the sun's rays.

08:35.140 --> 08:36.440
Saya...

08:43.790 --> 08:49.280
I wonder if Sei and Saya have been
going out for a long time...

08:49.890 --> 08:52.380
Saya is very pretty...

09:01.100 --> 09:02.600
What's the matter?

09:02.600 --> 09:03.810
You look so glum, Ichika!

09:03.810 --> 09:06.640
Manatsu, are you feeling better?

09:06.640 --> 09:07.580
Thank goodness!

09:07.580 --> 09:10.310
Yeah! Sorry for worrying you.

09:16.790 --> 09:19.690
You must be hungry. I'll go make you something.

09:19.690 --> 09:22.160
Yay! Thanks, Ma'am!

09:25.430 --> 09:27.730
Here, take it easy.

09:29.530 --> 09:31.330
Yum!

09:31.330 --> 09:34.100
I'm glad you're feeling better, Manatsu.

09:34.500 --> 09:37.770
I'm going to deliver some flowers.

09:37.770 --> 09:38.500
Okay!

09:39.310 --> 09:41.580
What are you making, Ichika?

09:41.580 --> 09:43.480
Tonight's dinner.

09:43.480 --> 09:45.550
Oh, you've got tutoring tonight.

09:45.550 --> 09:48.820
It's Sei this time, right?

09:48.820 --> 09:49.780
Right.

09:49.780 --> 09:54.160
I have to thank him for seeing me
when I was sick the other day...

09:54.160 --> 09:55.750
Sure, fine, I got it.

09:57.930 --> 09:59.220
Sei...

10:03.330 --> 10:04.630
Oww!

10:05.000 --> 10:05.970
Are you okay...

10:06.900 --> 10:08.390
I'm okay...

10:13.740 --> 10:15.040
Sei...

10:28.320 --> 10:33.120
To Sei, I'm just one of the students he tutors.

10:33.560 --> 10:36.160
That's all...

10:50.610 --> 10:52.670
This brings back memories.

11:02.690 --> 11:03.860
What are these?

11:03.860 --> 11:08.800
Ichika dear, please wear them
when you grow up.

11:12.170 --> 11:14.530
When I... grow up...

11:30.190 --> 11:31.780
They don't suit me at all...

11:35.790 --> 11:36.620
Coming!

11:52.640 --> 11:55.700
I bet Saya is still there.

11:56.080 --> 11:57.310
Come in.

11:58.110 --> 12:00.180
Sei, please come in!

12:00.180 --> 12:04.620
Ichika put her whole heart into
cooking you dinner, after all!

12:08.260 --> 12:09.790
During the Heiji Rebellion,

12:09.790 --> 12:14.000
Minamoto no Yoritomo
who had lost his father Yoshitomo,

12:14.000 --> 12:16.030
was sent to Izu under the Houjou clan,

12:16.030 --> 12:20.130
while his younger brother Yoshitsune was forced
to seek refuge in Kyoto's Kurama temple.

12:20.440 --> 12:24.940
Brothers... I hope they got along
like you and Kai...

12:25.910 --> 12:28.140
Yes, I guess.

12:28.140 --> 12:31.610
But after the destruction of the Heike
in the Battle of Dan-no-ura,

12:31.610 --> 12:35.880
he was chased down by his brother Yoritomo.

12:35.880 --> 12:38.110
Oh, really? I'm sorry...

12:50.500 --> 12:52.300
About the Houjou clan...

12:54.400 --> 12:57.100
He's looking at Saya's house next door!

13:00.980 --> 13:04.550
Sorry! I must not be over my cold yet.

13:04.550 --> 13:05.340
Take care.

13:07.880 --> 13:09.280
That's rare...

13:10.490 --> 13:12.720
You don't usually wear
something like that, Ichika.

13:16.360 --> 13:17.760
This isn't...

13:19.030 --> 13:21.000
This isn't...

13:23.870 --> 13:24.500
It hurts...

13:24.500 --> 13:25.700
Ichika, are you okay?

13:25.700 --> 13:27.540
Ichika, does it hurt?

13:27.540 --> 13:28.930
Ichika... Hey, Ichika!

13:29.840 --> 13:32.640
I'm so worthless...

13:32.640 --> 13:34.900
I'm no match for Saya!

13:36.410 --> 13:38.900
I'll go get the first aid kit!

13:40.380 --> 13:41.640
Hold still.

13:42.580 --> 13:45.290
It's not bleeding, but it's bruised.

13:45.290 --> 13:46.450
It must hurt.

13:46.450 --> 13:47.080
Are you okay?

13:48.190 --> 13:49.120
Yes...

14:06.370 --> 14:08.080
Thank you for the meal.

14:08.080 --> 14:09.980
It was delicious, Ichika.

14:09.980 --> 14:12.150
No, it was my pleasure.

14:12.150 --> 14:13.550
I was happy to.

14:14.950 --> 14:17.280
I'll keep a hold of this, then.

14:17.290 --> 14:20.890
Kai's really good at fixing these kinds of things.

14:20.890 --> 14:23.320
Yes, thank you.

14:24.490 --> 14:30.990
Um, can you change when
Kai comes tomorrow to after lunch?

14:32.730 --> 14:36.070
It's okay if you haven't fixed it by then!

14:36.570 --> 14:39.770
It shouldn't be a problem, but why?

14:40.840 --> 14:45.340
I can't tell him it's because I want it to be when
Saya is out on business or I can't concentrate...

14:47.550 --> 14:50.380
No, well... I'm sorry.

14:50.390 --> 14:52.490
Okay, I'll tell him.

14:52.490 --> 14:53.320
Later.

15:01.600 --> 15:05.630
It doesn't seem like Saya's left today.

15:05.630 --> 15:08.100
Ichika, the repairman is here!

15:08.800 --> 15:11.340
Hello! I'm the repairman!

15:11.340 --> 15:12.500
Kail

15:15.580 --> 15:17.370
Thank you very much!

15:29.290 --> 15:32.750
It's nice to do tutoring while it's still light out.

15:38.000 --> 15:38.590
Kail

15:39.500 --> 15:44.630
I couldn't ask you to tutor me
at the library... could I?

15:46.370 --> 15:49.000
See you later, Mother!

16:02.790 --> 16:03.720
Huh?

16:04.030 --> 16:05.590
But the library is this way.

16:05.590 --> 16:07.460
Don't worry about it.

16:18.410 --> 16:19.770
Why...

16:19.770 --> 16:22.370
We can't talk in the library, right?

16:22.840 --> 16:24.110
Oh...

16:24.110 --> 16:26.050
Please!

16:27.050 --> 16:28.780
A change of pace is good for you.

16:29.550 --> 16:31.710
I'll work on my own reports when I can.

16:43.360 --> 16:46.160
Is there something going on with your neighbor?

16:48.900 --> 16:50.100
Well, you see...

16:54.980 --> 16:59.040
Oh, I see. You love Sei, yeah...

17:00.620 --> 17:04.480
So do I. I really love him.

17:05.690 --> 17:07.550
...what would you do if I said that?

17:08.660 --> 17:10.060
Oh, Kai you silly!

17:11.060 --> 17:16.830
But I really do love him. I trust him.

17:17.800 --> 17:19.600
Keep it a secret from him, 'kay?

17:38.120 --> 17:41.820
I wonder why it's Sei and not you, Kai...

17:43.860 --> 17:46.390
You're a lot like Sei.

17:46.390 --> 17:48.160
I am?

17:49.300 --> 17:53.670
Now that I think about it,
you're kind of like Manatsu.

17:55.670 --> 17:58.010
You might be right about that.

17:58.010 --> 17:59.200
He's not like me!

18:00.680 --> 18:01.340
Probably...

18:01.340 --> 18:02.280
Manatsu...

18:03.210 --> 18:04.740
Perhaps.

18:08.020 --> 18:08.950
An ocean breeze?

18:17.330 --> 18:18.890
Oh no, the report!

18:18.890 --> 18:22.460
Ah well, I'll just have to rewrite it.

18:22.460 --> 18:24.100
No, I'll go find them!

18:24.100 --> 18:24.790
It's okay, really!

18:28.600 --> 18:30.200
Please, wait!

18:32.810 --> 18:33.830
Ichika...

18:39.310 --> 18:40.080
You'll use it?

18:41.450 --> 18:42.040
Yes.

19:17.420 --> 19:18.780
Don't worry!

19:19.320 --> 19:22.760
Normal people can't see us now.

19:33.630 --> 19:37.160
I guess I can't see them anymore.

19:42.780 --> 19:45.270
Saya? Why is she here?

19:58.430 --> 19:59.450
Ichika!

20:13.910 --> 20:14.640
Don't!

20:20.920 --> 20:22.110
Are you okay?

20:24.550 --> 20:26.790
Sorry for worrying you.

20:26.790 --> 20:28.480
That was quite a gust, wasn't it?

20:34.230 --> 20:35.630
Ichika...

20:35.630 --> 20:39.030
What did I just try and do?

20:41.240 --> 20:42.530
Ichika!

20:49.180 --> 20:51.280
Thank you for collecting the report.

20:51.280 --> 20:53.510
Visiting hours are already over...

20:57.380 --> 20:58.550
Let's go home.

21:03.460 --> 21:06.790
“I'm not going to use the Djinn's power again."

21:06.790 --> 21:08.560
"I don't won't use it, no matter what!"

21:09.360 --> 21:16.330
At that time I was overcome with fear
of the Djinn's power, and myself.

21:19.610 --> 21:20.370
Yes.

21:21.380 --> 21:23.710
I will proceed just as you say.

21:24.010 --> 21:24.910
Yes.

21:25.810 --> 21:27.940
No, nothing like that...

21:30.180 --> 21:33.120
Whether or not I will receive
a satisfactory answer...

21:34.360 --> 21:34.880
Yes.

21:40.330 --> 21:41.060
Yes.

21:42.800 --> 21:45.430
She has passed the point of no return.

21:47.700 --> 21:50.670


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.660 --> 23:20.790


23:20.790 --> 23:21.900


23:21.900 --> 23:24.000
It is a harsh reality when one opens one's eyes.

23:24.300 --> 23:28.000
But inside one's dreams is a tranquil solitude.

23:28.000 --> 23:29.670
On that day I came to realize

23:29.670 --> 23:34.730
that it requires a strong will
to stand up and face it.

23:34.740 --> 23:39.840
On the next Uta~Kata:
The Impulse of a Falling Flower
